  "verbalization": "Isoneobavachalcone is implicated in the biological activity of C8166 through a series of molecular interactions involving the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Isoneobavachalcone, which appears to act as a ligand that modulates the activity of this subunit. The evidence suggests that Isoneobavachalcone influences the function of the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which in turn affects the activity of C8166. The presence of multiple compounds that target the same subunit further supports the notion that Isoneobavachalcone may exert its effects through a shared mechanism, potentially by altering the subunit's function or by interacting with it directly. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta in the biological response to Isoneobavachalcone and its relationship with C8166.",
